393	/// The PostToolUse group that relays the finalized 🟩 metrics line as hook
394	/// output (`systemMessage` for the user, `additionalContext` for the model)
395	/// after a shell call — Codex's fallback for the rare host whose tool result
396	/// drops the merged stderr its exec layer normally carries. When the tool
397	/// result already carries the box, Codex and Devin stay silent while Claude
398	/// still gets the line as `systemMessage` only (its Bash result surfaces
399	/// stderr the user never sees), so a host that shows stderr does not print it
400	/// twice for the model. Codex's own entry lives in `codex_config`.
401	fn metrics_relay_group(exe: &Path, provider: Provider) -> Value {
402	    hook_group(
403	        format!(
404	            "{} run-hook metrics --provider {}",
